WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:05.900
Because of its massive reach and selection
of original content, Netflix can offer a little

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:07.240
something for everyone.

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:12.100
There's more to watch every month, making
it difficult to keep track of the best offerings.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:17.740
With that in mind, here are some of the best
series made by Netflix, for Netflix.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:20.220
13 Reasons Why

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:26.000
One of the saddest teen-oriented shows in
recent memory is also one of the best.

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:32.730
Based on the novel by Jay Asher, 13 Reasons
Why is a provocative, often unsettling examination

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:36.160
of bullying, mental illness, assault, trauma,
and suicide.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:43.120
The "13 reasons" of the title refer to audiotapes
recorded by a high school student named Hannah,

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:47.160
with each side detailing a different reason
why she took her own life.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:52.580
It's not for the faint of heart, but 13 Reasons
Why is definitely a must-watch.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.420
Orange Is the New Black

00:00:54.760 --> 00:01:00.460
"Women in prison" used to be the domain of
seedy movie theaters and late-night Cinemax.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:05.940
Not anymore: Orange Is the New Black is one
of the most wholly original and feminist series

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.060
in TV history.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:12.420
Based on Piper Kerman's memoir about being
an upper-middle-class white woman jailed for

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:17.310
a drug crime, the show has evolved into a
vast ensemble drama with a lot to say about

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.080
gender, race, and economic issues.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:25.020
It tells the stories of incarcerated women
as people, not just "criminals," and how they

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:29.580
form new families and learn more about their
own identities while locked up.

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:33.880
Clear your schedule, because once you start
you'll be binge-watching for hours.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:35.920
Stranger Things

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:41.780
It's no small feat that a show about children
in grave danger somehow gives viewers the

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:43.320
warm and fuzzies.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:44.830
That's the power of nostalgia.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:50.440
A wholly original science-fiction series with
its own deep mythology, rules, and a range

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:55.759
of fleshed-out characters, Stranger Things
is loaded with references to '80s sci-fi and

00:01:55.759 --> 00:01:58.620
horror, in part because it's set in the '80s.

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:03.990
More than anything, it feels like another
entry in that so-'80s genre of entertainment

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:10.100
about adventurous kids that adults could enjoy
too: inventive, dark, and completely entertaining.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:11.480
Never say die.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.040
BoJack Horseman

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:19.260
This is a cartoon set in some kind of alternate
universe where all kinds of animals have human

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.140
qualities and live among humans.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:26.760
Its main character is BoJack Horseman, a washed-up
actor who starred in a terrible '90s family

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:28.620
sitcom called Horsin' Around.

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:33.720
Yet in spite of all of this zaniness, BoJack
Horseman provides one of the most accurate

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:37.400
and heartbreaking portrayals of depression
ever put to screen.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:43.150
BoJack is a sellout who wants to make art,
but isn't sure if he can, and always self-sabotages

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:44.520
his own successes.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:47.840
Lemony Snicket's A Series of Unfortunate Events

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:54.420
While the 2004 adaptation of the kiddie goth
book series Lemony Snicket's A Series of Unfortunate

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:58.700
Events was certainly delightful, the problem
is that there was only one.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:04.120
There are multiple bestselling books about
the forever-doomed Baudelaire orphans, and

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:09.300
now they all finally get to come to life via
a Netflix original series.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:14.989
Neil Patrick Harris stars as the wicked Count
Olaf, an actor by trade who uses his access

00:03:14.989 --> 00:03:20.660
to wigs and makeup to worm his way into the
lives of the kids so he can steal their inheritance.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:26.629
The versatile Harris is perfectly cast as
Olaf, and he also sings the theme song, warning

00:03:26.629 --> 00:03:30.780
the viewer to stay away from the show because
it's just too bleak and troubling.

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:36.160
The dark and playful humor is balanced with
whimsical, dreamlike imagery, making a show

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:39.220
that's guaranteed to entertain all ages.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:40.820
Arrested Development

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:47.760
In 2013, Netflix aired its first revival of
a show originally produced on another network,

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:52.290
making quite a statement in the process: If
Arrested Development, a critically adored

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:56.849
cult hit that lurked near the bottom of the
ratings when it initially aired on Fox, could

00:03:56.849 --> 00:03:59.040
be revived, then anything could.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.900
It also proved Netflix was a major player
in entertainment, as an Arrested Development

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:09.190
revival had already been discussed at big
places like HBO and Showtime, with Netflix

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:10.780
ultimately winning out.

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:16.410
The show reunited the entire main cast to
create what's really a 13-episode movie.

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:20.729
Each episode focuses on the backstory of a
different main character and what they've

00:04:20.729 --> 00:04:22.669
been up to in the past decade or so.

00:04:22.669 --> 00:04:27.240
It's ridiculous, multi-layered, self-referential—and
astonishingly good.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:31.999
If you only watch one episode, watch the one
about Gob, in which he confuses the first

00:04:31.999 --> 00:04:36.979
friendship he's ever had for romantic attraction,
gets himself locked in a fake rock, tries

00:04:36.979 --> 00:04:41.599
and fails to raise bees, and becomes part
of the entourage of a pop star who writes

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:44.420
a song about how awful Gob is.

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:45.560
Flaked

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:48.900
How many Netflix shows is Will Arnett on,
anyway?

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:53.050
He's the voice of the title character on BoJack
Horseman, he plays a prominent figure in A

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:57.250
Series of Unfortunate Events, and he co-starred
in the Arrested Development revival.

00:04:57.250 --> 00:05:03.069
Arnett also co-created the quiet dramedy Flaked
about a recovering middle-aged alcoholic trying

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:07.080
to put his life back together after killing
another man while driving under the influence.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:12.300
His recovery includes making stools, fighting
with his best friend, and tooling around Venice,

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:13.600
California on his bike.

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:18.560
It's a sometimes poignant, sometimes funny
show about a numb guy in paradise trying to

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:21.409
take action but never quite getting there.

00:05:21.409 --> 00:05:24.980
Wait a second…is this just a live-action
BoJack Horseman?

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:26.800
W/ Bob and David

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:33.940
Mr. Show with Bob and David ran on HBO from
1995 to 1999 and became one of the most highly

00:05:33.949 --> 00:05:36.910
regarded sketch comedy shows of the '90s.

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:41.909
Many of its cast and writers went on to become
comedy icons, including stars David Cross

00:05:41.909 --> 00:05:47.039
and Bob Odenkirk, as well as Paul F. Tompkins,
Tom Kenney, and Scott Aukerman.

00:05:47.039 --> 00:05:51.620
Gathering all those talents together to make
more top-notch sketch comedy after nearly

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:57.149
20 years apart seemed impossible, but Netflix
was able to do it with the four-episode miniseries

00:05:57.149 --> 00:05:58.140
W/ Bob and David.

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:02.900
Time has passed but the magic has not, and
these sketches are worthy additions to the

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:04.120
Bob and David canon.

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:09.419
If you loved all the absurdity of the original,
you'll definitely get a kick out of the revived

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:09.920
series.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.000
Making a Murderer

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:18.520
Along with HBO's The Jinx, Netflix's Making
a Murderer reignited the public's fascination

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:19.800
with true crime stories.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:25.780
This exhaustive and extraordinarily compelling
series analyzes every possible aspect of the

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:32.179
2005 murder case for which Wisconsin man Steven
Avery was charged—and as the series shows,

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:34.280
a lot of things don't quite add up.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:35.820
Was evidence planted?

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:40.229
Were police out to frame Avery because he
was suing them for wrongful conviction and

00:06:40.229 --> 00:06:42.120
imprisonment for an earlier crime?

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:47.760
Did police coerce a confession out of Brendan
Dassey, Avery's accomplice and nephew?

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:52.559
Making a Murderer is equal parts riveting
and enraging, and its real-world struggle

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:54.580
is guaranteed to get you hooked.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:56.200
House of Cards

00:06:56.700 --> 00:07:02.300
Based on a British miniseries, House of Cards
details the slow, methodical, and deadly path

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:07.880
by which Southern politician Frank Underwood
seeks out and obtains the power he's so obsessed

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:08.380
with.

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:14.360
Over the course of several seasons, cold-blooded
Frank does whatever he needs to do to ascend

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:15.320
the government ladder.

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:20.340
Even if political dramas aren't usually your
thing, House of Cards is bound to suck you

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:20.840
in.

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:22.440
Master of None

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:28.600
Less a serial comedy series and more an anthology
of standalone episodes, Master of None is

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:31.999
definitely a unique addition to the Netflix
library.

00:07:31.999 --> 00:07:37.569
Comedian, actor, and writer Aziz Ansari and
his writing partner Alan Yang won an Emmy

00:07:37.569 --> 00:07:41.600
for this series, which is probably the first
to really capture the millennial point of

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:42.100
view.

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:48.020
It's thoughtful, wise, and even legitimately
touching—but also hilarious, because Ansari

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:49.180
can't help being funny.

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:50.620
The Crown

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:55.839
Quiet, slow-building stories about British
monarchs are nothing new to television—it's

00:07:55.839 --> 00:07:59.379
the bread and butter of PBS and the BBC, after
all.

00:07:59.379 --> 00:08:01.860
And yet The Crown is something entirely different.

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:09.089
Shot at a cost of $100 million, the most expensive
series in Netflix history, it's an extraordinarily

00:08:09.089 --> 00:08:15.699
ambitious project that aims to tell the complete
life story of Queen Elizabeth II, from childhood

00:08:15.699 --> 00:08:21.399
to coronation to the present day, as she struggled
to keep England together in the post-war years

00:08:21.399 --> 00:08:26.599
and learned how to be a stateswoman from the
incomparable Winston Churchill, portrayed

00:08:26.599 --> 00:08:27.599
by John Lithgow.

00:08:27.599 --> 00:08:31.970
Keep in mind that Elizabeth is still alive—but
she'd find it hard to be offended.

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:36.599
It's all done with an empathy and humanity
not generally given to larger-than-life figures,

00:08:36.599 --> 00:08:41.000
especially ones that can seem as cold and
distant as English monarchs.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:45.610
We see her grieve, we see her insecurities,
we even see her getting flirty with her husband

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:46.610
Prince Phillip.

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:51.829
The Crown is also absolutely gorgeous—the
set and costume design is so lush and spot-on

00:08:51.829 --> 00:08:54.820
that you could swear it was shot right in
Buckingham Palace.

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:56.340
The OA

00:08:57.060 --> 00:09:01.800
This sci-fi show is about a mysterious young
woman who re-appears after disappearing for

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:02.620
seven years...

00:09:02.900 --> 00:09:08.880
Only now she's covered in scars, calls herself
"The OA," and can see even though she used

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:09.520
to be blind.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:15.819
It's a dark, labyrinthine series about death,
the afterlife, science, violence, conspiracies,

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:17.180
and human spirituality.

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:20.360
In short, it gets deep, and it gets weird.

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:24.540
It's a good thing that Netflix doesn't charge
by the hour, because we'd all rack up huge

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:26.580
bills trying to figure out The OA.

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:28.140
Black Mirror

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:33.260
A dead TV series returning to life thanks
to rapidly spreading technology?

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:35.060
That sounds like an episode of Black Mirror!

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:41.540
Netflix revived Charlie Brooker's creepy British
sci-fi anthology series for six new stories.

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:46.259
They're all vaguely set in the very near future
and, like the original series, examine the

00:09:46.259 --> 00:09:51.500
often damaging effects of the place where
humanity and technology intersect, and how

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:56.380
that relationship affects our humanity and
dignity…for better or for worse.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.260
Santa Clarita Diet

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:04.420
Yeah, there are a lot of zombie shows on TV
right now, but Santa Clarita Diet has them

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:04.920
beat.

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:09.760
First of all, it's just as gory and disgusting
as The Walking Dead, but it's a lot funnier.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:14.959
Drew Barrymore and Timothy Olyphant star as
Sheila and Joel Hammond, Southern California

00:10:14.959 --> 00:10:19.000
real estate agents who hit a bit of a rough
patch in their marriage when Sheila turns

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:23.100
into a zombie with an insatiable desire for
human meat.

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:28.360
Naturally, she must turn to murder, but Joel
is on board, as is their teenage daughter

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:31.160
Abby and their macabre-obsessed neighbor.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:36.660
Sheila taking a huge bite out of life is a
great metaphor for choosing to live life to

00:10:36.661 --> 00:10:41.790
the fullest, but this is still a zombie show,
so there are plenty of gross-out moments.

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:47.050
No spoilers, but this is probably your only
chance to see the star of Never Been Kissed

00:10:47.050 --> 00:10:49.509
barf up a swimming pool's worth of sludge.

00:10:49.509 --> 00:10:51.180
"That was a crazy amount of vomit."

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.180
"Well, I'm not a medical expert.

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:55.399
So I can't say what the proper amount of vomit
is."

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:56.540
"It was a HUGE amount."

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:57.420
Daredevil

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:00.260
By day, Matt Murdock is a lawyer.

00:11:00.279 --> 00:11:04.930
By night, he cleans up New York's Hell's Kitchen
with his fists and fighting skills.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:10.720
The action sequences are intense, and Daredevil
lays waste to every thug he faces despite

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:11.220
his blindness.

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:16.379
Those scenes are almost as terrific as the
ones with Vincent D'Onofrio as the terrifying

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:17.379
villain Kingpin.

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:22.240
Put it all together, and you have one of the
best original action series on Netflix.

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:23.600
Even a blind man could see that.

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:25.240
Jessica Jones

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:28.900
Is Jessica Jones the first superhero psychological
drama?

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:34.319
It's a comic book and superhero show without
the usual trappings—you rarely see Jessica

00:11:34.319 --> 00:11:36.060
exhibit her amazing abilities.

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:41.000
Instead, it focuses on the ramifications of
how she's used those powers in the past.

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:45.630
In many ways, it's less of a superhero show
and more about a young woman trying to forge

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:48.820
her own identity while struggling to leave
her past behind.

00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:51.680
She just happens to be super-strong.

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:53.440
Luke Cage

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:58.500
This show marks Netflix's first spin-off,
focusing on the character portrayed by Mike

00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:00.300
Colter on Jessica Jones.

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:11.120
It's another Marvel series that reflects the
real world and its culture, history, and race

00:12:11.139 --> 00:12:12.139
relations.

00:12:12.139 --> 00:12:17.860
Luke Cage is a human story about a superhero
trying to navigate a world in which he sometimes

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:22.490
feels like he doesn't fit in, which makes
a great allegory about a young man trying

00:12:22.490 --> 00:12:26.000
not to get swallowed up by the underbelly
of urban society.

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:27.280
Thanks for watching!

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:30.040
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:32.489
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

